 the circumstances probably  we will adapt our way of working and i  intend  to continue to try to develop a strong  preparation for each european council  we have experienced the last month  smaller formats smaller video conference  in preparation of some  some difficult topics we used this tool  smaller formats for example in order to  prepare  our position regarding china we did the  same regarding  turkey in the eastern ireland we think  it's a it's a  an effective approach in order to be  certain that we have  a space for real interactivity political  interactivity  among among the the leaders then  today we agreed formally  our conclusions on the digital and  single market  this is a very strong signal this is a  very  important step that we are making today  european  foreign  foreign  we had a short update about  the negotiations the the ongoing  process of negotiations with the  european parliament  in order to implement what we have  decided in july  the mff the on resources and  the recovery fund we will have the  occasion in the next days  uh to be involved in order to try to  make progress we know that there are  some difficult topics  between the member states and with the  european parliament that we need to  solve we note that we know that our  agreement in july  was a political package and it's very  essential to be able  as soon as possible to deliver to  implement what we have  decided it's a question of credibility  that i feel  a strong political will to make progress  and to be able to implement the mff  and the recovery fund but will continue  to work  very hard in order to reach this goal  and finally  just one word about brexit just an  information session we had the occasion  to have an  update by ursula and also an analysis  by the irish prime minister  but we didn't open the debate today  because we  you know that we'll have the occasion uh  in october during our next meeting  to have a more substantial exchange of  views  and we will take into consideration the  possible developments between today and  the next  european council we trust the commission  we trust michelle barnier  we have a clear european position we are  united  we are very calm we have expressed very  clearly  the last week what we think about the  current situation and we will have the  occasion  in october to tackle this important  topic  it is  thank you have the floor madam president  merci  thank you very much um it was very good  that  the leaders decided to devote time to  our collective response to the covered  pandemic the epidemiological situation  is worrying  so we must stay very focused to  avoid a return to the dire situation we  experienced last spring  and we can only overcome both the  pandemic and its consequences  if we work together member states and eu  institutions  and therefore this debate was very  deep diving and three things from this  debate stand out first of all  progress on vaccines is the key to a  long-term solution to this crisis  we're making good progress the  commission has already concluded  two advanced purchase agreements and it  is negotiating  five more and we are in discussions with  four more companies so this is on a good  track  because through this these advanced  purchase  agreements we are investing  in production capacities right now  to ensure that the access to the  vaccines is  there for the european citizens so  ramping up the production lines  buying now raw material and all the  necessary ingredients  that you need to ramp up then the  production once we have the vaccine  the second point is the vaccine strategy  whom to vaccinate first the commission  has put forward a blueprint for vaccine  plan before the summer break and good  news is that it has been adopted now  with the health security committee so we  can move  on with council recommendation based on  this blueprint  and thirdly we discuss that we must do a  better job in coordinating our  assessment and the measures 