nk you yeah yes we we had a very  short distinction on this topic  because it was important for us to  listen to the update  presented by the german  president of uh of the council by angela  merkel  and it's not a secret it's not a  surprise  we know that it's key to implement as  soon as possible what we have decided  uh in july and we know that the creation  of rule of law  is a difficult topic it was in july a  difficult topic it was a sensitive topic  but in july  we took the decision to make the  traditionality with the governance and  with  the creation of a rule of law and then  we will continue in the next days to  work very hard  uh with the member states but also with  the european parliament  on this uh on this topic uh i know that  it will be a difficult decision it will  be a difficult debate  but i think and i hope uh that we will  have  together all the member states with uh  the members of the open parliament it  will  that will have the common political will  in order to find  a solution because it's very important  for the european future  to be able to ratify as soon as possible  in the national parliaments but also to  get the agreement of the european  parliament  can be very brief indeed it was a report  of the german presidency  on i would call it the state of  negotiations with the european  parliament at the moment being  these negotiations are ongoing charles  michel has mentioned  all the diffi different and difficult  issues  there was no in-depth discussion because  it is  work and progress and when there is a  result to be debated  then this will be the time to do to go  in depth  thank you  please you're next yes hi uh good  afternoon i have a question  for each uh president and first for  president vandalia and i just wondered  uh  you will meet boris johnson tomorrow  a video conference with him and i just  want to know what's going to be the most  important thing will you address  specifically the internal market bill  first and foremost or will you start  negotiating  looking where we can go on the free  trade talks  and i would also like to know what your  assessment your latest assessment is  on the progress that we now have seen so  far  and then i have a question for council  president michelle  and it's about u.s president trump who  has tested positive  for covet and i just wondered what  lessons we can draw from uh  from this on how we should deal with the  pandemic  thank you madam president yes um  thank you uh indeed uh there are two  strands work strands at the moment being  the one is the implementation of the  withdrawal agreement  and as you know the draft internal  market bill is heavily contradicting  some of the provisions in this  withdrawal agreement  mainly when it comes to the protocol of  ireland northern ireland  and as you know we asked the  uk government to withdraw this within a  month  this didn't take place so we launched an  infringement procedure  this is going its way the infringement  procedure  process is a part of the dispute  settlement  of the withdrawal agreement and the  second trend indeed are the overall  negotiations and  my phone called it actually is going to  be a video conference with boris johnson  uh will serve to take stock of the  negotiations at that  time and to have a look at  the time coming up i will then report to  council  in sum your third part of the question  is we want a deal  because we think it is better to have a  deal as  neighbors also on top in these  covet times with devastating impact on  the economies  it is good to have a deal but not at any  price  and mainly the topic of the level  playing field  how can we make sure that it exists  between both economies  and the question of fisheries are very  difficult so  we will see how we'll progress on that  yes about donald trump  test it positive of course  we all wish with him a speedy recovery  but of course i will not personally i  will not give  a health advice  we have another question now for  gavin lee from bbc news gavin  hi hello can you hear me okay yes please  state your question first  for both of you could you just explain a  little why  president lukashenko wasn't included in  the sanctions given that the uk and  canada believe that this was a point  to include him in sanctions and a second  brief  uh follow-up question on brexit um on  the eu  uk trade deal i know we've heard about  your your conversation with boris  johnson tomorrow  uh president on the line but could you  also give a sense you know the uk  side are still saying they can see a  light at the end of the tunnel  can you see a light at the end of the  tunnel on talks  maybe about uh the sanctions on on  belarus we took the decision to  implement and today it's done like i  announced yesterday today it's done we  implemented  this entrance we have a list with 40  names and you know that  in europe there's a clear process in  order to prepare the list what we did  there was indeed a debate uh on on  lucashenko on the list or not and we  took the decision after the debate  to follow the list uh proposed uh  at the the ministerial uh level but of  course we will follow uh  closely the situation and you know that  we are in favor  of an inclusive dialogue on belarus and  in belarus  and we hope that it will be possible for  the oec  to play a real and efficient role in  order to improve the situation  so um on the uk  question um we have in germany saying  that goes when villa is in weak and  translated it's more or less where there  is a will  there is a way and we should not forget  that we have made progress on many many  different fields  but of course the most difficult ones  are still completely open  and this is mainly also the question of  the level playing field  because this is the question of fairness  so if you want full access to the single  market  you have to a certain amount abide  to the rules that are the fairness rules  within  the single market and questions like  state aid for example  are questions of fairness and of  competitiveness  advantages that you give to companies or  not and there are rules that have to be  worked out we also would have to work on  a mechanism  where over time we  when things change there's an alignment  and if there are problems and  difficulties there must be a dispute  settlement  mechanism so you see from my words  there's still  a lot of work to do but it is as i say a  matter of fairness  and if you want to have the full access  to the single market  these fairness rules must apply and  therefore this is so difficult  but overall where there is a will there  is a way  so i think we should intensify  the negotiations because it's worth  working hard on it a second point on the  withdrawal agreement  as it is it can be implemented  implemented  and i call again on everybody to  really work hard to implement it is so  important  to have this clarified we have the whole  text we have the possibilities now  to sort out the difficulties in on the  island of  ireland and in good faith keeping  the good friday agreement this is very  important this can be done too  we'll take a last question now from uh  from sam flanging  from the ft sam are you with us  i am thanks very much uh i'm afraid of a  follow-up on brexit again  um madame bottom line you mentioned the  idea of the need to intensify  negotiations  um does that imply that you do see the  prospect of now entering a  negotiating tunnel or going sumarin  in order to um to reach the possibility  of that deal  and i want to just more broadly what  what are the key things you'll be asking  boris johnson when you speak to him what  do you want to hear from him  i mean do you believe that the uk  government is united and actually  wanting a trade deal  thank you so um  i don't like the term tunnel to be  honest because uh  it's it's a weird association so  intensify is we're running out of time  it's  uh i think uh around 100 days till the  end of the year  so uh it's worth to step up now  um as always in these uh um  vcs or telephone calls  i go in them in an open mind we want to  take stock  and we want to exchange positions  so i will not communicate to boris  johnson beforehand via media  what my expectations are  thank you and this concludes our press  conference of today may i remind you  that the leader's agenda which was  proposed by the president of the  european council  is on our website so please consult that  now  thanks a lot and see you soon  you

